-    "content": "# [Guide] Legacy Tracker Migration and Cutover Runbook\n\n## Overview\n\nOrganizations seeking to escape SaaS paywalls, Jira seat taxes, and single-vendor agent lock-in require a safe, deterministic migration path. Legacy project management tools often store data in proprietary formats, making manual migration prone to data loss, dropped comments, and broken ticket linkages.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban provides a battle-tested **7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol** (`docs/CUTOVER.md`) designed for migrating from legacy issue trackers (such as Jira, Vibe Kanban, or self-hosted boards) to \ud83d\udc4dkanban with zero data loss and minimal operational disruption.\n\n---\n\n## The 7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    P1[\"Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness & Schema Alignment<br/>- Deploy target stack, configure Multi-Card Auth<br/>- Run healthchecks and verify checksums\"]\n    P2[\"Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform<br/>- Place legacy tracker in maintenance mode<br/>- Capture baseline snapshot\"]\n    P3[\"Phase 3: Extraction & Markdown Normalization<br/>- Ingest JSON/XML export<br/>- Run Unicode Surrogate & Paste-Jacking pipeline\"]\n    P4[\"Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration & Linking<br/>- Populate UOG spine & typed object_links<br/>- Generate redirect aliases\"]\n    P5[\"Phase 5: Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates<br/>- Entity counts, Link Auditor, Markdown fidelity,<br/>ACL parity, MCP health, SLA latency\"]\n    P6[\"Phase 6: DNS Cutover & Traffic Switch<br/>- Point domain to \ud83d\udc4dkanban Caddy ingress\"]\n    P7[\"Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring & Rollback Window<br/>- 7-day read-only fallback window\"]\n\n    P1 --> P2\n    P2 --> P3\n    P3 --> P4\n    P4 --> P5\n    P5 -->|Certified PASSED| P6\n    P6 --> P7\n```\n\n![Standalone to Production Compose Export](images/27-standalone-compose-export.png)\n\n### Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness and Schema Alignment\n- Deploy target \ud83d\udc4dkanban production stack.\n- Configure Multi-Card Authentication cards to match source identity providers (OIDC/SAML/LDAP).\n- Run migration pre-flight checks: `uv run kanban-ctl ops healthcheck` and verify source export snapshot checksums (`sha256sum -c manifest.sha256`).\n\n### Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform\n- Place the legacy tracker instance into read-only maintenance mode.\n- Notify engineering teams and pause active CI/CD webhooks.\n- Capture baseline snapshot of source database.\n\n### Phase 3: Extraction and Markdown Normalization\n- Extract work items, cycles, modules, pages, stickies, and attachments via source tracker export APIs.\n- Pass all textual descriptions and comments through the \ud83d\udc4dkanban **Canonical Markdown Pipeline**:\n  - Rejects Unicode lone surrogates.\n  - Strips hidden DOM paste-jacking sequences.\n  - Converts legacy HTML into clean, standardized CommonMark.\n\n### Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration\n- Ingest normalized objects into the PostgreSQL Universal Object Graph (`kanban_migrator`).\n- Translate legacy issue references (`PROJ-123`) into canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban identifiers while creating redirect aliases.\n- Establish typed `object_links` for all parent-child relationships, sub-issues, and blockers.\n\n### Phase 5: The Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates\nBefore DNS can be redirected, the migration must pass all 6 automated verification gates:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Gate1[\"Gate 1<br/>Entity Parity\"] --> Gate2[\"Gate 2<br/>Link Auditor\"]\n    Gate2 --> Gate3[\"Gate 3<br/>Markdown Fidelity\"]\n    Gate3 --> Gate4[\"Gate 4<br/>ACL Parity\"]\n    Gate4 --> Gate5[\"Gate 5<br/>MCP Health\"]\n    Gate5 --> Gate6[\"Gate 6<br/>SLA Latency\"]\n    Gate6 --> Cutover[\"Ready for Live Cutover\"]\n```\n\n| Gate # | Verification Gate | Success Threshold |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Entity Count Parity** | 100% match across issues, states, cycles, modules, comments, and attachments. |\n| **2** | **Object Link Auditor** | Zero orphaned links, cross-tenant leaks, or invalid hierarchy cycles. |\n| **3** | **Markdown Fidelity** | 100% of descriptions render valid Markdown; zero unparsed HTML tags. |\n| **4** | **Principal & ACL Parity** | All users, groups, and permissions map accurately to \ud83d\udc4dkanban roles. |\n| **5** | **MCP Surface Health** | All 24 MCP tools return clean schemas and pass handshake benchmarks. |\n| **6** | **Performance Latency** | Board view initial load under 100ms; REST API p95 latency under 50ms. |\n\n### Phase 6: DNS Cutover and Traffic Switch\n- Update internal DNS records or reverse proxy routing (e.g. Caddy / Nginx) to point domain `kanban.example.com` to the \ud83d\udc4dkanban production ingress (`edge_net`).\n- Restart agent background workers with updated MCP endpoint URLs.\n\n### Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring and Rollback Window\n- Maintain legacy tracker instance in read-only state for a 7-day observation window.\n- Monitor real-time WebSocket connection stability and activity logs.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Import Studio (`/admin/imports`)\n\nTo streamline cutover from Plane workspaces to \ud83d\udc4dkanban without custom extraction scripts, \ud83d\udc4dkanban includes a native **Migration Import Studio** accessible at `/admin/imports` (and `/settings/mcp` -> Migration Studio tab).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph PlaneImportPipeline[\"Migration Import Studio Pipeline\"]\n        Upload[\"Step 1: Upload Plane Export Bundle<br/>(File upload or paste raw JSON)\"] --> Parse[\"JSON Schema Validation<br/>Verify projects, states, issues, cycles, modules, comments, members\"]\n        Parse --> Metrics[\"Step 2: Entity Detection & Metrics Cards<br/>Live counts across all 7 entity types\"]\n        Metrics --> DryRun[\"Step 3: Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation<br/>Idempotency checks, state mapping preview, conflict detection\"]\n        DryRun --> Live[\"Step 4: Execute Live Migration<br/>Atomic PostgreSQL transaction (kanban_migrator)\"]\n        Live --> Verify[\"Step 5: Post-Import Integrity Audit<br/>Run Invalid Object Link Auditor on imported graph\"]\n    end\n```\n\n![Migration Import Studio Step 1](images/49-admin-plane-import-studio.png)\n\n![Migration Studio Dry-Run Simulation](images/71-plane-migration-dry-run.png)\n\n### Key Migration Capabilities:\n1. **Direct JSON Ingestion:** Accepts standard Plane export bundles via direct drag-and-drop file upload or pasting raw JSON.\n2. **Real-Time Entity Metric Cards:** Displays instant counts for detected Projects, States, Issues, Cycles, Modules, Issue Comments, and Members.\n3. **Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation:** Simulates the complete import without writing to the database. Displays state mapping translations, identifies potential duplicate keys, and computes idempotency diffs.\n4. **Atomic Transactional Import:** Live migrations execute within an atomic transaction. If any entity fails validation or violates an object graph invariant, the entire migration rolls back cleanly, leaving existing data untouched.\n5. **Universal Link Synthesis:** Automatically establishes typed `PARENT_OF`, `BLOCKS`, and `ATTACHED_TO` object links corresponding to source Plane relationships.\n\n---\n\n## Emergency Rollback Procedure\n\nIf a critical business blocker occurs during the cutover window:\n1. **Revert DNS:** Immediately restore DNS routing to the legacy tracker cluster.\n2. **Delta Capture:** Run `uv run kanban-ctl cutover verify` / inspect `activity_records` since cutover to extract any tickets updated in \ud83d\udc4dkanban during the live window.\n3. **Reconcile:** Re-apply the delta diff into the source tracker to ensure zero data loss.\n\n![Workspace Home After Successful Cutover](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n"
+    "content": "# [Guide] Legacy Tracker Migration and Cutover Runbook\n\n## Overview\n\nOrganizations seeking to escape SaaS paywalls, Jira seat taxes, and single-vendor agent lock-in require a safe, deterministic migration path. Legacy project management tools often store data in proprietary formats, making manual migration prone to data loss, dropped comments, and broken ticket linkages.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban provides a battle-tested **7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol** (`docs/CUTOVER.md`) designed for migrating from legacy issue trackers (such as Jira, Plane, GitHub Issues, Linear, or self-hosted boards) to \ud83d\udc4dkanban with zero data loss and minimal operational disruption.\n\n---\n\n## The 7-Phase Live Cutover Protocol\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    P1[\"Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness & Schema Alignment<br/>- Deploy target stack, configure Multi-Card Auth<br/>- Run healthchecks and verify checksums\"]\n    P2[\"Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform<br/>- Place legacy tracker in maintenance mode<br/>- Capture baseline snapshot\"]\n    P3[\"Phase 3: Extraction & Markdown Normalization<br/>- Ingest JSON/XML export<br/>- Run Unicode Surrogate & Paste-Jacking pipeline\"]\n    P4[\"Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration & Linking<br/>- Populate UOG spine & typed object_links<br/>- Generate redirect aliases\"]\n    P5[\"Phase 5: Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates<br/>- Entity counts, Link Auditor, Markdown fidelity,<br/>ACL parity, MCP health, SLA latency\"]\n    P6[\"Phase 6: DNS Cutover & Traffic Switch<br/>- Point domain to \ud83d\udc4dkanban Caddy ingress\"]\n    P7[\"Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring & Rollback Window<br/>- 7-day read-only fallback window\"]\n\n    P1 --> P2\n    P2 --> P3\n    P3 --> P4\n    P4 --> P5\n    P5 -->|Certified PASSED| P6\n    P6 --> P7\n```\n\n![Migration Import Studio - Desktop Light](images/slice4-imports-1440x900-light.png)\n\n### Phase 1: Pre-Cutover Readiness and Schema Alignment\n- Deploy target \ud83d\udc4dkanban production stack using `thumbs-up-kanban:latest` or 5-network Compose.\n- Configure Multi-Card Authentication cards to match source identity providers (OIDC, SAML, LDAP, Passkeys).\n- Run migration pre-flight checks: `uv run kanban-ctl ops healthcheck` and verify source export snapshot checksums (`sha256sum -c manifest.sha256`).\n\n### Phase 2: Read-Only Freeze of Source Platform\n- Place the legacy tracker instance into read-only maintenance mode.\n- Notify engineering teams and pause active CI/CD webhooks.\n- Capture baseline snapshot of source database and uploaded attachments.\n\n### Phase 3: Extraction and Markdown Normalization\n- Extract work items, cycles, modules, pages, stickies, and attachments via source tracker export APIs or database dumps.\n- Pass all textual descriptions and comments through the \ud83d\udc4dkanban **Canonical Markdown Pipeline**:\n  - Rejects Unicode lone surrogates (`0xD800 <= ord(c) <= 0xDFFF` -> `INVALID_UTF8_SURROGATE`) before byte encoding.\n  - Strips hidden DOM paste-jacking sequences and malicious script injection vectors.\n  - Converts proprietary AST trees (Atlassian Document Format ADF, HTML, Markdown) into standardized UTF-8 CommonMark.\n\n### Phase 4: Universal Object Graph Hydration\n- Ingest normalized objects into the PostgreSQL Universal Object Graph under `kanban_migrator` authority.\n- Translate legacy issue references (`PROJ-123`, `JIRA-101`, `GH-88`, `ENG-42`) into canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban identifiers while registering permanent `issue_key_aliases` records.\n- Establish typed `object_links` for all parent-child relationships, sub-issues, and blockers.\n\n### Phase 5: The Six Non-Bypassable Verification Gates\nBefore DNS can be redirected, the migration must pass all 6 automated verification gates:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Gate1[\"Gate 1<br/>Entity Parity\"] --> Gate2[\"Gate 2<br/>Link Auditor\"]\n    Gate2 --> Gate3[\"Gate 3<br/>Markdown Fidelity\"]\n    Gate3 --> Gate4[\"Gate 4<br/>ACL Parity\"]\n    Gate4 --> Gate5[\"Gate 5<br/>MCP Health\"]\n    Gate5 --> Gate6[\"Gate 6<br/>SLA Latency\"]\n    Gate6 --> Cutover[\"Ready for Live Cutover\"]\n```\n\n| Gate # | Verification Gate | Success Threshold | Exact Audit Check |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Entity Count Parity** | 100% match across issues, states, cycles, modules, comments, and attachments | Verify `extractEntityCounts` matches source metrics exactly |\n| **2** | **Object Link Auditor** | Zero orphaned links, cross-tenant leaks, or invalid hierarchy cycles | `POST /api/v1/admin/object-links:audit` returns 0 invalid links |\n| **3** | **Markdown Fidelity** | 100% of descriptions render valid Markdown; zero unparsed HTML tags | CommonMark AST validator with lone-surrogate rejection |\n| **4** | **Principal & ACL Parity** | All users, groups, and permissions map accurately to \ud83d\udc4dkanban roles | Verified user mapping JSON matches active principals |\n| **5** | **MCP Surface Health** | All 24 MCP tools return clean schemas and pass handshake benchmarks | `/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, `/mcp/admin` initialize with 200 OK |\n| **6** | **Performance Latency** | Board view initial load under 100ms; REST API p95 latency under 50ms | Realtime WebSocket `/ws` probe RTT < 50ms |\n\n### Phase 6: DNS Cutover and Traffic Switch\n- Update internal DNS records or reverse proxy routing (Caddy or Nginx) to point domain `kanban.example.com` to the \ud83d\udc4dkanban production ingress (`edge_net`).\n- Restart agent background workers with updated MCP endpoint URLs (`/mcp/agent`).\n\n### Phase 7: Post-Cutover Monitoring and Rollback Window\n- Maintain legacy tracker instance in read-only state for a 7-day observation window.\n- Monitor real-time WebSocket connection stability, activity logs, and link health in Admin Diagnostics.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Import Studio (`/admin/imports`)\n\nTo streamline cutover from legacy issue trackers to \ud83d\udc4dkanban without authoring bespoke extraction scripts, \ud83d\udc4dkanban provides a native **Migration Import Studio** accessible at `/admin/imports` (and through the Administration navigation under Data Management).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph ImportPipeline[\"Migration Import Studio Pipeline\"]\n        Upload[\"Step 1: Select Source & Input Bundle<br/>(Plane, Jira, GitHub Issues, Linear, or Portable)\"] --> Parse[\"JSON Schema Validation<br/>Verify projects, states, issues, cycles, modules, comments, members\"]\n        Parse --> Metrics[\"Step 2: Entity Detection & Metrics Cards<br/>Live counts across all 7 entity types\"]\n        Metrics --> DryRun[\"Step 3: Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation (dry_run=true)<br/>Idempotency checks, state mapping preview, conflict detection\"]\n        DryRun --> Live[\"Step 4: Execute Live Migration (dry_run=false)<br/>Atomic PostgreSQL transaction (kanban_migrator)\"]\n        Live --> Verify[\"Step 5: Post-Import Integrity Audit<br/>Run Invalid Object Link Auditor on imported graph\"]\n    end\n```\n\n![Migration Import Studio Multi-Source Tabs](images/slice4-imports-multi-source-tabs.png)\n\n### Studio Controls and Backend Contracts\n\nThe Migration Import Studio exposes five core operational controls backed by `/api/v1/admin/imports`:\n\n1. **Source Platform Selector (`source`):**\n   Controls the source schema parsing and normalization rules. Allowed options are `plane` (Plane JSON bundle), `jira` (Jira Cloud/Server JSON or REST dump), `github` (GitHub Issues JSON dump), `linear` (Linear JSON export), and `portable` (canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban `.tar.gz`). Selecting a source automatically configures the appropriate entity mapping pipeline and custom field extractors.\n\n2. **Target Workspace and Project (`workspace_slug`, `project_key`):**\n   Specifies the destination tenant and project key for all imported entities. If omitted, the importer creates or binds to the default workspace and project declared inside the bundle. Imported issues receive canonical sequence numbers under the target project key (e.g. `KAN-1`, `KAN-2`).\n\n3. **Dry-Run Simulation Toggle (`dry_run`):**\n   When enabled (`dry_run=true`), the importer executes a non-destructive simulation against a database savepoint. It calculates entity diff counts, validates referential links, checks user mappings, and generates an `ImportDiffReport` without committing rows to PostgreSQL. When disabled (`dry_run=false`), the import runs inside an atomic database transaction that commits only upon full validation success.\n\n4. **Custom User Mapping JSON (`user_map`):**\n   A JSON dictionary mapping source usernames, legacy IDs, or email addresses to canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban user accounts (e.g. `{\"legacy_user\": \"adamoutler@gmail.com\", \"usr_123\": \"engineer@example.com\"}`). Unmapped users fall back to the system administrator or are created as external inactive principals depending on organizational configuration.\n\n5. **Legacy Key Alias Preservation (`IssueKeyAlias`):**\n   Whenever legacy issues are imported from Jira, GitHub, or Linear, their historical keys (e.g. `JIRA-101`, `GH-88`, `ENG-42`) are automatically recorded in the `issue_key_aliases` table. Requests to legacy URLs or API endpoints return `HTTP 308 Permanent Redirect` pointing to the canonical \ud83d\udc4dkanban issue key.\n\n![Migration Import Studio - Desktop Dark](images/slice4-imports-1440x900-dark.png)\n\n![Migration Studio Dry-Run Simulation](images/71-plane-migration-dry-run.png)\n\n---\n\n## Step-by-Step Operator Guide: Executing a Production Migration\n\nFollow this operational procedure to perform a clean cutover using the visual studio:\n\n1. **Navigate to the Studio:** Log in as a user with `SERVER_ADMIN` credentials, satisfy the AAL2 WebSudo prompt, and open `/admin/imports`.\n2. **Select the Source:** Click on the tab matching your source platform (`Plane`, `Jira`, `GitHub Issues`, or `Linear`).\n3. **Upload Export Payload:** Drag and drop your source export file or paste raw JSON into the input textarea. The studio instantly displays live metric cards showing detected Projects, States, Issues, Cycles, Modules, Comments, and Members.\n4. **Supply User Mapping (Optional):** If user handles differ between the source tracker and \ud83d\udc4dkanban, expand the User Mapping section and paste your JSON mapping dictionary.\n5. **Run Stage 1 Dry-Run Simulation:** Click **Simulate Dry-Run**. The backend processes the bundle with `dry_run=true` and returns an itemized diff summary detailing entities to be created and any potential conflicts.\n6. **Execute Live Migration:** Once the simulation is verified, click **Import Live**. The backend executes the atomic transaction (`dry_run=false`). A progress indicator tracks hydration progress until completion.\n7. **Verify Post-Import Health:** Switch to `/admin/link-auditor` and click **Start Comprehensive Scan** to verify zero broken object links. Request a migrated issue using its legacy key in your browser to confirm HTTP 308 redirection to the new canonical URL.\n\n---\n\n## Emergency Rollback Procedure\n\nIf an unrecoverable business blocker arises during the live cutover window:\n1. **Revert Ingress DNS:** Immediately restore DNS routing to the legacy tracker cluster.\n2. **Delta Capture:** Query the PostgreSQL immutable activity ledger (`activity_records`) to extract all work items, comments, and state changes committed during the cutover window.\n3. **Reconcile State:** Re-apply the captured delta entries back into the source tracker to ensure absolute data continuity with zero dropped updates.\n"
